{"cluster_id": "C-2803", "topic": "The system.cas_mounts columns are started_at and expires_at; the _ms", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B046-055", "B048-063"], "canonical_claim": "The system.cas_mounts columns are started_at and expires_at; the _ms suffix remains on internal MountLease millisecond fields, persisted \"sat\"/\"eat\" body keys, cas-inspect JSON keys, holder_expires_at_ms, and log fields because those values are raw epoch milliseconds rather than DateTime64(3) columns. `MountLease` fields and related `system.cas_log` detail keys retain `started_at_ms` and `expires_at_ms` because their values are raw epoch milliseconds; the suffix is semantically accurate even where a display column uses `DateTime64(3)`.", "issue_ids": ["T8"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t4-report.md#L1-L21", ".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t8-report.md#L3-L24"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2804", "topic": "The 05012_cas_mounts_typed_columns.reference remains unchanged because the query orders...", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B046-056"], "canonical_claim": "The 05012_cas_mounts_typed_columns.reference remains unchanged because the query orders expires_at, server_uuid, and started_at in the same alphabetical order as the old names; a missing renamed column would reduce the result from three rows to two and fail the reference.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-03-cas-obscure-names/t4-report.md#L23-L30"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2805", "topic": "seedCompletedRemoving recovers and retains the predecessor runtime while its", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B048-067"], "canonical_claim": "`seedCompletedRemoving` recovers and retains the predecessor runtime while its catalog row is `Live`; absent and replacement fence-race fixtures therefore exercise real `Pool::invalidateRemovedCatalogLife` behavior and force name-based recovery away from the predecessor life.", "issue_ids": ["7.5a", "T5"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75a-reconciler-fix-r1-report.md#L3-L15"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2806", "topic": "The immutable runtime identity has the shape RootNamespace ->", "target": "architecture/mounts-and-leases", "member_ids": ["B049-018"], "canonical_claim": "The immutable runtime identity has the shape `RootNamespace -> RefNameSlot -> RefTableRuntime(NamespaceLifeId, admitted_fence_generation)`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog/task-5-checkpoint75c-runtime-cpp-report.md#scope-and-outcome"]}
